# What a terminal's page does with each keydown (grid-input.js's keydownAction): Farhelm's contract for
# which keys reach the program at keydown and which are left to the browser's text input. Change it only on
# purpose: edit it by hand and review the diff (its generator,
# the old web GUI's `grid-input-tables.js`, went with that GUI; read it at commit 24bc0580).
# ["p", id, pattern] lines name each pattern by an id taken from its SHA-1. A pattern's position
# mods * 4 + altGraph * 2 + deadKeyBefore (mods: 1 Shift, 2 Alt, 4 Ctrl, 8 Meta) holds one letter:
#   a pass
#   b pass, dead key pending
#   c send cancelled
#   d pass cancelled
#   e page-up cancelled
#   f page-up cancelled, dead key pending
#   g page-down cancelled
#   h page-down cancelled, dead key pending
#   i ignore
#   j ignore, dead key pending
#   k select-all
#   l select-all, dead key pending
# [keyCode, key, code, pattern id on Linux x86_64, pattern id on MacIntel, pattern id on Win32]
